.El
.Sh BUILD OPTIONS
.Nm
builds with CMake 3.21 or later and GCC or Clang with C23 support.
Ninja is the supported generator; on Windows only Clang with the GNU-style
driver is supported.
The build produces
.Pa libxft.a ;
consumers link the
.Ql xft::xft
target, which carries the freestanding flags.
.Bl -tag -width "XFT_BUILD_GENTABLE"
.It Dv XFT_LIBC
Build against a libc instead of freestanding.
Default off.
.It Dv XFT_NATIVE
Compile with
.Fl march=native Fl mtune=native .
Default on; forced off when cross compiling.
.It Dv XFT_LTO
Link-time optimization.
Default on.
.It Dv XFT_FAST_MATH
Compile with
.Fl ffast-math .
Default on.
.It Dv XFT_SANITIZE
AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
Forces
.Dv XFT_LIBC
on and
.Dv XFT_LTO
off.
Default off.
.It Dv XFT_STRICT_ARCH
Compile only the architecture backends of the host.
Default off.
.It Dv XFT_RT
Use the
.Nm
entry point, which calls
.Fn xft_main .
When off, the libc entry point and the program's
.Fn main
are used and
.Dv XFT_LIBC
is forced on.
Default on.
.It Dv XFT_BUILD_TESTS
Build the unit tests, always sanitized.
.It Dv XFT_BUILD_FUZZ
Build the fuzz targets, always sanitized.
.It Dv XFT_BUILD_BENCH
Build the benchmarks, never sanitized.
Linux only.
.It Dv XFT_BUILD_GENTABLE
Build
.Nm gentable ,
the generator of the
.Xr xft_xid 3
tables.
.It Dv XFT_BOOTSTRAP_XID
Build the library without the xid module and regenerate its table from
.Pa DerivedCoreProperties.txt
in the source root.
Forces
.Dv XFT_BUILD_GENTABLE
on.
See
.Xr xft_xid 3 .
.El
.Pp
Warnings are always errors.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <xft.h>

void	xft_main(const t_any *__restrict__ const sp)
{
	(void)sp;
	xft_exit(0);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xft_alloc 3 ,
.Xr xft_io 3 ,
.Xr xft_rt 3 ,
